        "Microstructure_Text": {
          "original": "exhibit a tempered martensite microstructure with a comparable average grain size of around 60 μm... small amounts of austenite phase... distributed randomly along the martensite laths. The volume fractions of austenite are measured to be 8.3±0.8%... high densities of nanoscale spindle precipitates were observed... STEM-EDS maps reveal the co-segregation of Ni and Ti, indicating the formation of (Ni, Ti)-rich precipitates... D024-ordered structure, characteristic of the Ni3Ti-type η phase... number density of Ni3Ti precipitates in the Cu-free steel is 2.5×10^23 m^-3, with an average radius of 3.1 nm and a volume fraction of 3.1%.",
